    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d512-a1">

                <pb facs="0597" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg501"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ambassador</hi>: In due time I received your note
                    of the 27th ultimo, relative to the delivery of Mrs. Mattie D. Rich, whose
                    extradition was granted by the Government of the United States.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say to your excellency that I have transmitted your
                    said note to the governor of the State of Chihuahua, that he may communicate it
                    to the judge who is trying Mrs. Rich’s case, with the necessary recommendations
                    that the indications therein contained may be properly regarded.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
